 238:/home/reo/Documents/Repository/sca-2026/lib/crypto_kem/hqc128/pqclean/fft.c **** 
 239:/home/reo/Documents/Repository/sca-2026/lib/crypto_kem/hqc128/pqclean/fft.c **** /**
 240:/home/reo/Documents/Repository/sca-2026/lib/crypto_kem/hqc128/pqclean/fft.c ****  * @brief Evaluates f on all fields elements using an additive FFT algorithm
 241:/home/reo/Documents/Repository/sca-2026/lib/crypto_kem/hqc128/pqclean/fft.c ****  *
 242:/home/reo/Documents/Repository/sca-2026/lib/crypto_kem/hqc128/pqclean/fft.c ****  * f_coeffs is the number of coefficients of f (one less than its degree). <br>
 243:/home/reo/Documents/Repository/sca-2026/lib/crypto_kem/hqc128/pqclean/fft.c ****  * The FFT proceeds recursively to evaluate f at all subset sums of a basis B. <br>
 244:/home/reo/Documents/Repository/sca-2026/lib/crypto_kem/hqc128/pqclean/fft.c ****  * This implementation is based on the paper from Gao and Mateer: <br>
 245:/home/reo/Documents/Repository/sca-2026/lib/crypto_kem/hqc128/pqclean/fft.c ****  * Shuhong Gao and Todd Mateer, Additive Fast Fourier Transforms over Finite Fields,
 246:/home/reo/Documents/Repository/sca-2026/lib/crypto_kem/hqc128/pqclean/fft.c ****  * IEEE Transactions on Information Theory 56 (2010), 6265--6272.
 247:/home/reo/Documents/Repository/sca-2026/lib/crypto_kem/hqc128/pqclean/fft.c ****  * http://www.math.clemson.edu/~sgao/papers/GM10.pdf <br>
 248:/home/reo/Documents/Repository/sca-2026/lib/crypto_kem/hqc128/pqclean/fft.c ****  * and includes improvements proposed by Bernstein, Chou and Schwabe here:
 249:/home/reo/Documents/Repository/sca-2026/lib/crypto_kem/hqc128/pqclean/fft.c ****  * https://binary.cr.yp.to/mcbits-20130616.pdf <br>
 250:/home/reo/Documents/Repository/sca-2026/lib/crypto_kem/hqc128/pqclean/fft.c ****  * Note that on this first call (as opposed to the recursive calls to fft_rec), gammas are equal to
 251:/home/reo/Documents/Repository/sca-2026/lib/crypto_kem/hqc128/pqclean/fft.c ****  * meaning the first gammas subset sums are actually the subset sums of betas (except 1). <br>
 252:/home/reo/Documents/Repository/sca-2026/lib/crypto_kem/hqc128/pqclean/fft.c ****  * Also note that f is altered during computation (twisted at each level).
 253:/home/reo/Documents/Repository/sca-2026/lib/crypto_kem/hqc128/pqclean/fft.c ****  *
 254:/home/reo/Documents/Repository/sca-2026/lib/crypto_kem/hqc128/pqclean/fft.c ****  * @param[out] w Array
